xpilot-ng (4.7.3+r7-1~noble1) noble; urgency=high

  * Build from the v4.7.3-r7 release.
  * Security: a server could overwrite the client's stack through the map
    data package its map names, by giving a file in it a name longer than
    the buffer it was read into. The package extractor is rewritten: names
    are limited to the characters real packages use, the file count and
    unpacked size are capped, and a refused package leaves nothing behind.
  * Map textures download again. The mirror the maps point at redirects
    http to https, which the old downloader could not follow; it now uses
    libcurl, restricted to http and https with a size cap.
  * Build-Depends on libcurl4-gnutls-dev.

 -- bartromb <bart.rombaut@gmail.com>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:17:47 +0200

xpilot-ng (4.7.3+r6-1~noble1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Build from the v4.7.3-r6 release.
  * Do not install mapconvert.py: it is Python 2, does not parse under
    Python 3, and its shebang names an interpreter that a stock Ubuntu does
    not have. It stays in the source for a later port.
  * Take VeraMoBd.ttf and FreeSansBoldOblique.ttf from ttf-bitstream-vera
    and fonts-freefont-ttf rather than shipping copies of them.

 -- bartromb <bart.rombaut@gmail.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 20:53:29 +0200

xpilot-ng (4.7.3+r5-1~noble1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging of the revival fork, built from the v4.7.3-r5 release.
    Upstream XPilot NG last released in 2010; this tree ports it to CMake,
    SDL2 and SDL2_mixer and fixes the defects that stopped it building and
    running on current systems.
  * Sound is enabled: the audio path is SDL2_mixer, and the sample files are
    installed with it.
  * Binaries install to /usr/games per policy, with their data in
    /usr/share/xpilot-ng where the binaries are compiled to look for it.

 -- bartromb <bart.rombaut@gmail.com>  Sat, 30 Aug 2026 17:10:00 +0200
